{
 "author_name": "HeavyMap",
 "author_url": "https://heavymap.com/journey",
 "content": [
  {
   "children": [
    "working-paper, architecture, framework"
   ],
   "tag": "aside"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A working paper written on 2026-10-18, published nearly as written. Local file paths, private repository names and personal names have been removed."
   ],
   "tag": "blockquote"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Status:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " accepted 2026-10-18 (the owner). Linear ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-269"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ". Universal back-end setting. Not a fifth product name."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Every dataset carries a ",
    {
     "children": [
      "publish_visibility"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " value in the dataset inventory (",
    {
     "children": [
      "Spreadsheets/02-dataset-inventory-v4.csv"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "). The build reads that value and emits only what the setting allows. This is a screening and shipping rule, not a licence ledger and not a UI copy guide."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Values"
   },
   "children": [
    "Values"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "public"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Default. Allowlisted fields may ship in public output."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "restricted"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: The dataset was paid for, or licence permission is unconfirmed. Values do not ship in public output."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "withheld"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: No values ship. Whether the dataset is named in public output is ",
      {
       "children": [
        "withheld_disclosure"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "internal_only"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Never shipped and never mentioned in public output. Used only for internal checks."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "restricted"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " is the paid-or-unconfirmed-licence class. It is not the same as ",
    {
     "children": [
      "withheld"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (a screening choice on a known source) or ",
    {
     "children": [
      "internal_only"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (never mentioned)."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Existing inventory rows were left ",
    {
     "children": [
      "public"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " when this column was added. Agents do not reclassify a row to ",
    {
     "children": [
      "restricted"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " unless a packet says so."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Restricted-list-(not-in-git)"
   },
   "children": [
    "Restricted list (not in git)"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Public files may say that a restricted dataset list exists. They do not list the restricted datasets, their paid status, or their licence papers."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The list itself is gitignored:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "live file (local only): ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Spreadsheets/restricted/RESTRICTED-DATASETS.csv"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "committed template (headers only): ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Spreadsheets/restricted/RESTRICTED-DATASETS.template.csv"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "committed README: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Spreadsheets/restricted/README.md"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The live file is the place for dataset ids, restriction kind (",
    {
     "children": [
      "paid"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " or ",
    {
     "children": [
      "unconfirmed_licence"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ") and provenance notes. No pulled rows, no licence keys, no secrets."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Future private repo."
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " Restricted atlas data and the infrastructure that holds it are planned for a private ",
    {
     "children": [
      "ia-restricted"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " repository. Until that exists, pinned restricted inputs stay in git-ignored local data (not published) on machines that are allowed to hold them (today: Deb). Cursor cloud VMs cannot see local data (not published) (it is off git) and cannot reach ArcGIS, so they cannot run a full jurisdiction rebuild or the repeat-run proofs."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "withheld-disclosure-(open;-interim-default)"
   },
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "withheld_disclosure"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (open; interim default)"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A second setting, ",
    {
     "children": [
      "withheld_disclosure"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", chooses whether a ",
    {
     "children": [
      "withheld"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " dataset appears as a manifest-level gap entry (",
    {
     "children": [
      "manifest_entry"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ") or is omitted (",
    {
     "children": [
      "none"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "). the owner has not closed this. ",
    {
     "children": [
      "Interim default: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "manifest_entry"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", marked interim. Do not treat the interim default as a decision."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Field-level-withholding"
   },
   "children": [
    "Field-level withholding"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A ",
    {
     "children": [
      "public"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " dataset can still have individual fields screened (owner names, owner mailing addresses, legal descriptions, other personal fields). Those fields are never read into public output (HARD-RULES 2, D-13). The data-gaps ledger names the field and the screening rule (",
    {
     "children": [
      "withheld_screened"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "); it does not carry values."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Dossiers will signal that identifying information is held. Wording is a front-end and business decision tied to logged-in and paid tiers. This document does not write that copy."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Repo-split-(timing-pending)"
   },
   "children": [
    "Repo split (timing pending)"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Keep the mechanism in this repository for now. Move the back end to an ",
    {
     "children": [
      "industrial-atlas"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " repo as soon as practical, leaving ",
    {
     "children": [
      "heavymap"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " (local and GitHub) dedicated to the front end. Timing is pending the owner confirmation."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Prepared with Claude (Anthropic) · model Claude Opus 5.5 · 2026-11-18"
     ],
     "tag": "em"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "tag": "hr"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "heavymap-journey/1\nid: JP-0087\ntype: working-paper\nsection: systems\nevidence_date: 2026-10-18\nseq: 20"
   ],
   "tag": "pre"
  }
 ],
 "description": "working-paper, architecture, framework",
